--- CLIPPING CENSUS (MEASURED) ---
container max   : 16383 DN. NOT the usable white level (15360) -- these are
                  two different numbers for two different purposes and both are right:
                  15360 bounds the noise model's calibrated range, 16383 is what
                  "this sample is pinned" means. Do not unify them.
ever clipped    : 0.0000% of pixels (3 of 8241504) clipped in at least one frame
always clipped  : 0.0000% of pixels (3 of 8241504) pinned in EVERY frame
                  ^ these carry ZERO focus information. M26 measured 616 such px on
                  coffee-bubbles reading cross-frame focus contrast 1.0000, the
                  metric's MAXIMUM, against 0.5398 median on never-clipped px --
                  because 85.9% of them have f_min exactly 0 (inside a uniformly
                  clipped blob the gradient is identically zero) while f_max is 52x
                  typical (the blob edge crosses them in another frame). Discipline
                  29 does NOT protect against this: it preferred cross-frame
                  contrast to focus magnitude, but on a pinned pixel BOTH read
                  their maximum, so they fail in the same direction.
                  NOTE 109MSDCF and 119MSDCF are two of the four stacks with NO
                  saturation, and 109 is also the quietest photometrically (M24).
                  A clean result on them is systematically weaker evidence than it
                  looks.

